# ChefVoice local LLM (the "Gemma" model-selector option).
#
# One-time import of the local GGUF into Ollama:
#   ollama create chefvoice-gemma -f backend/Modelfile.gemma
#
# Then start/keep Ollama running (`ollama serve`) and pick "Gemma" in the
# assistant's model selector. The model is a 26B MoE (~4B active/token) at
# Q4_K_M (~16 GB); it won't fully fit a 12 GB GPU, so Ollama automatically
# offloads the overflow layers to system RAM. Ollama reports this model as
# tool- and thinking-capable; the agent sends `think: false` for fast, clean
# spoken replies (its native tool-calling still works with thinking off).
#
# Update the FROM path if your GGUF lives elsewhere.
FROM C:/models/google_gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf

# Modest context keeps KV-cache memory down so more layers fit in VRAM. The
# voice agent only sends the system prompt + last few turns, so 8k is plenty.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0.4
PARAMETER stop "<end_of_turn>"
